; Build-network resilience only. Nothing here changes WHAT gets installed —
; the lockfile is still the single source of truth — only how patiently npm
; waits for the registry.
;
; Added after a Railway build died on `npm ci` with ERR_SOCKET_TIMEOUT. npm
; defaults to 2 retries with a 60s ceiling, which is not much cover when the
; builder's connection to the registry stalls mid-download on a dependency
; tree this size.
;
; This makes a transient stall less likely to fail the deploy. It cannot fix a
; real registry outage or a genuinely broken network — if a build fails this
; way twice in a row, the problem is upstream, not here.
fetch-retries=5
fetch-retry-factor=2
fetch-retry-mintimeout=20000
fetch-retry-maxtimeout=180000
fetch-timeout=600000
